# React Hook Form Best Practices

This document outlines best practices for working with React Hook Form in our project, focusing on performance, validation, and TypeScript integration.

## Form Setup

- Use `useForm` hook for form state management and validation
- Implement defaultValues to initialize form fields
- Define proper TypeScript interfaces for form data
- Use form context for complex, nested forms
- Set mode to appropriate validation trigger (onBlur, onChange, onSubmit)

## Form Registration

- Use register method for basic form fields
- Implement Controller component for controlled components
- Apply consistent naming convention for form fields
- Use watch selectively to avoid unnecessary rerenders
- Take advantage of form arrays for dynamic fields

## Validation

- Define validation schemas with Zod, Yup, or Joi
- Use resolver to integrate schema validation
- Implement custom validation functions for complex cases
- Display validation errors clearly to users
- Use error mapping to transform error messages
- Handle async validation properly

## Performance

- Avoid unnecessary rerenders with proper field registration
- Use `shouldUnregister` option consciously
- Implement conditional form fields efficiently
- Use FormProvider for complex forms
- Consider field arrays for dynamic form elements
- Don't overuse watch function

## TypeScript Integration

- Define proper types for form values
- Use generic typing with useForm<FormValues>()
- Leverage TypeScript for validation schemas
- Apply proper typing for error messages
- Use type inference where possible

## Form Submission

- Implement proper loading states during submission
- Handle submission errors gracefully
- Reset form after successful submission when appropriate
- Provide clear feedback to users
- Use handleSubmit to process form data 
